  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Main front is now making its way across eastern\nNC this hour with band of showers and an isolated thunderstorm\nnow focused east of Highway 17. All precipitation should work\noffshore by midnight, and until then overall environment does\nnot support an ongoing severe threat. Lingering low clouds are\nlikely into the overnight hours before a surge of dry air ushers\nin mainly clear skies to start Saturday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A more seasonably dry airmass will be ushered \nin for the weekend behind the front. Expect a return to mostly \nsunny skies and highs in the upper 60s to low 70s Sat, then \ncooler yet for Sun with 60-65. Lows will be in the 40s, with \nsome 30s for some of the normally colder spots. We will have to \nmonitor the temp forecast for any frost concerns Sunday morning.",
